    pr_ref:  # 4593
    description: "**Origin / provenance.** Surfaced 2026-06-09 while formalizing the `not_duplicate_of` links between WI-madal (run crashes on unreadable file) and WI-himas-gohif (META: top-level CLI exception handler). Adding `--add-not-duplicate-of` on one item did not make the relationship visible from the other item, which prompted an audit of how the tracker stores, mutates, reads, and renders `not_duplicate_of`.\n\n**The invariant (violated).** `not_duplicate_of` is semantically SYMMETRIC (\"A and B are distinct\"), but its storage, write path, and display are all DIRECTIONAL, with nothing reconciling the two. A link recorded on item A is invisible from item B on several surfaces.\n\n**Evidence (consumer audit of `.not_duplicate_of`):**\n- Storage: `models.py:381-383` — per-item directional `list[str]`.\n- Write: `cli.py:767-771` (`--add-not-duplicate-of`) writes the edited item only; no mirror. Changelog diff (`cli.py:672`) logs one side.\n- Dedup suppression (the field's PRIMARY consumer) reads SYMMETRICALLY: `validation.py:832` and `embeddings.py:353` both test `id_b in a.not_dup OR id_a in b.not_dup`. So a one-sided link DOES suppress near-dup warnings either way — the field is functionally correct for dedup.\n- Display reads DIRECTIONALLY: text `show` (`_format_item_full`, `cli.py:221-222`) and JSON (`_item_to_dict`, `cli.py:274`, shared by `show --json` and `list --json`).\n- Web UI (`serve.py`) and TUI (`tui.py`) do NOT render `not_duplicate_of` in EITHER direction.\n\n**Contrast — why this field is the odd one out.** `duplicate_of` is correctly directional (A folds into canonical B; mirroring would be wrong). `isbefore` is correctly directional and even ships an inverse-convenience flag (`--add-blocked-by`, `cli.py:843`). `not_duplicate_of` is the only conceptually-symmetric relation and the only one with neither mirroring nor symmetry handling — reads like an oversight, not a directed-edge design.\n\n**Facets / sub-gaps (so a future implementer does not re-derive them):**\n1. Display: a one-sided link is invisible from the reverse item in text `show` / `--json`; web UI + TUI show it in neither direction.\n2. No reverse-lookup affordance: there is no `list --not-duplicate-of <ID>` query. The hygiene use case (\"looking at B, what is judged distinct-from-B and why?\") is not queryable.\n3. Rationale locality: the \"why distinct\" justification lives in a discussion note on whichever side authored it; a bare link does not carry it. (This is why the WI-madal / WI-himas mirror was a NOTE, not just a link.)\n4. Concurrency: the store is a per-item op-log (`store.py:1381-1486`, per-item add/remove ops), compiled by Lamport-ordered per-element replay (`compile_ops`, `store.py:645-666,902`), merged by git-union of append-only logs (`sync.py`). So even an atomic two-sided mirror-write can be torn apart on a concurrent branch merge — per-element reconciliation is invariant-blind.\n5. Delete: the inbound-reference sweep on delete (`_cmd_delete` / INV-vudit, `cli.py:1271-1322`) covers `isbefore` ONLY — not `not_duplicate_of`. So deletes already leave dangling `not_duplicate_of` refs (detected but not repaired by `validation.py:707`).\n\n**Recommended fix (lowest burden, guarantees symmetry).** A single read-time resolver `resolved_not_duplicate_of(item, ts)` that unions both directions, called by EVERY surface (text show, `_item_to_dict`, serve, TUI, and any future consumer). Storage stays single-sided (the naturally-emitted state), so there is no two-sided write invariant to maintain across add/remove/delete/merge, and nothing to desync on a concurrent merge. Symmetry becomes a function of the data rather than an invariant maintained across two copies.\n\n**Rejected alternatives.**\n- Render-only patch (fix `show` / `--json` only): does not compose — must be re-implemented per surface, leaves web UI / TUI blind, no reverse-lookup, regresses for any new surface.\n- Mirror-on-write: must also un-mirror on remove AND extend the delete sweep to `not_duplicate_of` AND back-fill existing one-sided links AND still needs a repair pass, because a per-item op-log cannot keep a two-sided invariant convergent under concurrent merges (local write-atomicity does not imply merge convergence).\n- Pair-keyed single-record representation (the \"true one atom\"): correct, but a brand-new representational pattern for a tracker where every relation (parent / isbefore / duplicate_of / not_duplicate_of) is currently a per-item list field; not worth it for this alone.\n\n**Optional add-ons** (file separately if pursued): a `list --not-duplicate-of <ID>` reverse-lookup; a `validation.py` rule that REPORTS asymmetric `not_duplicate_of` pairs (riding the existing dangling-ref machinery) rather than maintaining them on write.\n\n**Severity.** Low / minor. Dedup suppression — the field's primary purpose — already works (symmetric read). Impact is discoverability during a dedup / tracker-hygiene sweep, plus latent-trap risk for any future direct reader of `item.not_duplicate_of`. Not a release blocker.\n\n**Context thread.** WI-madal (`not_duplicate_of` WI-himas-gohif) and WI-himas-gohif carry the originating links plus the fail-open-vs-graceful-closed hazard note."  # 4593
    fields:  # 4593
      statement: "not_duplicate_of is semantically symmetric (A distinct-from B implies B distinct-from A) but the tracker stores, mutates, and displays it directionally on the editing item only; a link recorded on one item is invisible from the other on text show, JSON, web UI, and TUI. Only the dedup validators read both directions; there is no mirroring, no shared symmetric read-resolution, and no symmetry repair."  # 4593
      root_cause: "not_duplicate_of is modeled as a per-item directional list[str] (models.py:381-383) like the genuinely-directed duplicate_of and isbefore, but its semantics are symmetric. Only the dedup-suppression consumers (validation.py:832, embeddings.py:353) read both directions; every display surface reads the edited item only, so one-sided storage is never reconciled into a symmetric view."  # 4593
